-- title:
--   Prime Hecke set at q meets exactly q+1 unit cosets
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$. Let $q$ be a prime and assume $R$ is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ (orders maximal for inclusion among orders) with the relative index of the additive group of $R$ in that of $\Lambda_1$ equal to $N$, and assume $q\nmid N$. Let $q'$ be a prime with $q'\neq q$ such that $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible precisely when $q\in v$ fails and $q'$ lies in $v$. Write $\widehat{R}$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox R`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele, and let $U_R$ be the stabiliser of $\widehat{R}$ in the unit group of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$. Then the set of cosets in $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f})^{\times}/U_R$ having a representative $g$ with $g\in\widehat{R}$, $q\,g^{-1}\in\widehat{R}$, $g^{-1}\notin\widehat{R}$ and $q^{-1}g\notin\widehat{R}$ is finite of cardinality $q+1$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Hecke set $\mathcal{T}_q(R)$ of an Eichler order of level prime to $q$, in a definite quaternion algebra split at $q$, is a union of exactly $q+1$ right cosets of the idelic unit group; classically it is the degree of the Hecke correspondence $T_q$ on the class set of $R$, equivalently the common column sum of the Brandt matrix $B(q)$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, for the combinatorics of the coset graph and for the identification of the Hecke matrix attached to `primeHeckeSet` acting on the class set.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_natCard_setOf_exists_mem_primeHeckeSet_quotientMk_eq_eq_succ_of_prime.lean

